     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>When doing a local_install, is it possible to specify option for the local installation? For instance, I want to install the vimcom R package (which is not on CRAN) into my packrat repo. I&#39;ve used local repos for this by doing the following <br><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mkdir </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/R/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages<br>cd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/R/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages<br>wget http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimr/vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimr/vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242491929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2f5Ohi05pELngLUkckH5D1\">www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimr/vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz</a></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xzvf vimcom_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6.tar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gz</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>Then in my project with packrat enabled:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">packrat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">set_opts</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">local</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">repos </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;~/R/packages&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>packrat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">install_local</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;vimcom&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>I am assuming this calls install.packages() at some point in install_local with the repos parameter set? In any case, for installing vimcom I need to actually specify the some additional configure options on my Mac OS X (<a href=\"http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimcom.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimcom.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242491929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Xjhol2qLYNcE-gB8TZjhj\">http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimcom.html</a>). Normally, I would install this way:</div><div><br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">install</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;source&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> configure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">args</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;--enable-clientserver, --x-includes=/opt/X11/include --x-libraries=/opt/X11/lib&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> repos </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>Is there a way to set these configuration options with install_local?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Fong</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
